---
import Landing from '../layouts/Landing.astro';
---

<Landing
	lang="en"
	title="enodia"
	description="Know what you are running, and how long it has left. Service inventory and lifecycle/EOL monitoring for your infrastructure."
>
	<main>
		<h1>enodia</h1>
		<p class="tagline">Know what you are running, and how long it has left.</p>
		<span class="status">pre-1.0 — no tagged release yet</span>

		<p class="pitch">
			enodia asks your deployed services what version they're running, checks
			those versions against vendor lifecycle calendars, and tells you what's
			already dead, what's dying, and where your fleet has drifted apart. You
			describe your services once — enodia handles the rest.
		</p>

		<!--
			No install one-liner yet on purpose: install.sh pulls from GitHub
			Releases, and no tagged release exists as of this writing. Publishing
			a `curl | sh` line here before one ships would just 404 for anyone
			who ran it. Swap this block in once a real release lands.
		-->
		<pre><code>git clone https://github.com/EpicMorg/enodia.git</code></pre>

		<nav class="links">
			<a href="https://docs.enodia.sh/">Documentation</a>
			<a href="https://github.com/EpicMorg/enodia">GitHub</a>
			<a href="/ru/">Русский</a>
		</nav>
	</main>
	<footer>
		enodia is <a href="https://github.com/EpicMorg/enodia/blob/master/LICENSE">AGPL-3.0-or-later</a>.
	</footer>
</Landing>
